#N canvas 20 20 2500 1900 12;
#X text 20 20 e_plate -- the reverb's plate \, one of e_verb's three engines and the one it starts on (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): Dattorro's plate in vanilla boxes \, from his Effect Design Part 1 (JAES 1997) \, figure 1: a bandwidth low-pass and four diffusers into a tank of two halves \, each a modulated allpass \, a delay \, a damping low-pass \, the decay and an allpass \, feeding the other. Both sides' seven output taps are summed: mono. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: c_kit's \$0 \, for the throw. arg 2: e_verb's \$0 \, for its input. In: the sends \, on e_verb's \$2-in. inlet: want <1 or 0> \, size <0-100> and damping <0-100> \, from e_verb. Out: the reverb alone \, thrown to c_kit's \$1-out. outlet: 1 or 0 as its switch~ turns., f 70;
