#X text 1640 900 size is the tank's decay \, worked out so the plate's tail measures the time e_verb's size reads: 0.5 s at 0 to 10 s at 100 \, even in ratio. Each half of the tank takes two decays \, worked out for a half of 0.3016 s \, which measures true where its delays add to 0.36 \; the second allpasses' diffusion follows the decay and 0.15 \, from 0.25 to 0.5 \, as the paper has it. damping is the tank's low-passes \, the pole 0.959 d / (d + 23): 0 at 0 \, 0.66 at 50 and 0.78 at 100 \, so the tail darkens as freeverb's does at the same damping. Each starts at 50 in its boxes: c_steps tells c_kit every value at load. Delays are the paper's samples at 29761 Hz \, in ms. The gain is the paper's 0.6 on the taps \, with what matches its level to the other engines., f 50;
#X text 1640 1200 The engine's own: the input at its gain while it is wanted and 0 once it is not \, so a type changed away from rings out on what it already holds \; e_tail turns its switch~ on while it is wanted and off once its tail has died \, clearing its delay lines \, and the outlet tells e_verb \, whose own switch~ is on while any engine is., f 50;
